[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a complete, copy‑and‑paste‑ready recipe for loading a **single `.pmtiles`** archive (vector, raster or raster‑DEM) into a MapLibre GL JS map.

---

## 1️⃣ Install the PMTiles helper library

MapLibre itself does not understand the `pmtiles://` protocol, but the **`pmtiles`** npm package ships a tiny protocol handler that does the heavy lifting (range‑requests, header parsing, caching).

```bash
# From your project root
npm install pmtiles   # or yarn add pmtiles
```

> **Tip:** The current `pmtiles` package (≥ 3.0.0) works with every MapLibre version (v3‑v6). It automatically adapts to the new `addProtocol` signature introduced in v4.

---

## 2️⃣ Register the protocol **once** (before any map is created)

```js
// src/pmtiles-setup.js  (or any module that runs at app start)
import * as pmtiles from 'pmtiles';
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

// Create the protocol instance
const pmtilesProtocol = new pmtiles.Protocol();

// Register it under the name "pmtiles"
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', pmtilesProtocol.tile);

// (Optional) clean‑up when the last map is destroyed
export const removePmtilesProtocol = () => {
  maplibregl.removeProtocol('pmtiles');
};
```

> **Why only once?** `addProtocol` registers a global handler. Registering it inside a React component’s render loop, for example, would add the same handler many times and can cause memory‑leaks or duplicate network requests.

---

## 3️⃣ Reference the archive in a **style source**

You have three possible source types:

| Type | When to use | Example `type` value |
|------|-------------|----------------------|
| Vector tiles | Streets, boundaries, POIs, etc. | `"vector"` |
| Raster imagery | Satellite, orthophoto, custom PNG/JPEG tiles | `"raster"` |
| Raster‑DEM (elevation) | Terrain, hillshade, 3‑D terrain | `"raster-dem"` (add `"encoding": "terrarium"` or `"mapbox"` ) |

### Minimal style object (inline)

```js
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import './pmtiles-setup';   // <-- makes sure the protocol is registered

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',               // id of the <div>
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {
      // -------------------------------------------------
      // 1️⃣ Vector example (most common)
      // -------------------------------------------------
      myVector: {
        type: 'vector',
        // The URL can be either:
        //   • pmtiles://https://example.com/tiles.pmtiles   (recommended)
        //   • https://example.com/tiles.pmtiles            (works too, but you lose the "pmtiles://" prefix that makes the protocol explicit)
        url: 'pmtiles://https://my-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/world.pmtiles'
      },

      // -------------------------------------------------
      // 2️⃣ Raster example (satellite imagery)
      // -------------------------------------------------
      // myRaster: {
      //   type: 'raster',
      //   url: 'pmtiles://https://my-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/satellite.pmtiles',
      //   tileSize: 256          // optional, defaults to 256
      // },

      // -------------------------------------------------
      // 3️⃣ Raster‑DEM example (terrain)
      // -------------------------------------------------
      // elevation: {
      //   type: 'raster-dem',
      //   url: 'pmtiles://https://my-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/elevation.pmtiles',
      //   encoding: 'terrarium'   // or "mapbox"
      // }
    },

    // -------------------------------------------------
    // Layers that draw from the source
    // -------------------------------------------------
    layers: [
      {
        id: 'water',
        type: 'fill',
        source: 'myVector',
        'source-layer': 'water',   // exact layer name inside the PMTiles file
        paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
      },
      {
        id: 'roads',
        type: 'line',
        source: 'myVector',
        'source-layer': 'road',
        paint: {
          'line-color': '#777',
          'line-width': 1
        }
      }
      // add more layers (labels, buildings, etc.) as needed
    ]
  },

  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});
```

#### Key points in the source definition

| Property | What to set | Why |
|----------|-------------|-----|
| `type`   | `"vector"` / `"raster"` / `"raster-dem"` | Tells MapLibre how to interpret the tiles. |
| `url`    | `pmtiles://https://…/myfile.pmtiles` | **Never** use the `tiles:` array for PMTiles. `url:` makes the protocol read the archive’s internal TileJSON (min/max zoom, bounds, attribution, etc.). |
| `source-layer` (per‑layer) | Exact name of the layer inside the archive (e.g. `water`, `road`, `building`) | Vector tiles can contain many layers; you pick which one to draw. |
| `encoding` (raster‑dem only) | `"terrarium"` or `"mapbox"` | Required so MapLibre can decode elevation values. |
| `tileSize` (raster only) | `256` (default) or `512` | Matches the size you used when generating the tiles. |

---

## 4️⃣ Host the `.pmtiles` file where it can be fetched with **HTTP Range** requests

| Provider | How to enable |
|----------|---------------|
| **AWS S3** | Upload the file, make it public (or use signed URLs). S3 already supports `Range`. Set `Cache‑Control: public, max-age=31536000` and `Access‑Control‑Allow‑Origin: *`. |
| **Cloudflare R2** | Same as S3 (S3‑compatible API). Put behind Cloudflare CDN for extra caching. |
| **GitHub Pages** | Keep the file < 100 MiB (GitHub’s static‑site limit). Enable CORS via a `CNAME` or a `*.github.io` site that serves the file. |
| **Netlify / Vercel / any static host** | Verify that the host returns `Accept‑Ranges: bytes`. Add CORS headers (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`). |
| **Local dev** | `python -m http.server 8000` works, but you must add `--bind 0.0.0.0` and a small script to set the CORS header, or use `serve -c-1` from the `serve` npm package. |

> **CORS note:** Browsers will issue a **pre‑flight** request for the `Range` header. The server must answer with `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Range` (or `*`). Most CDNs add this automatically when you enable CORS, but double‑check the network tab if tiles fail to load.

---

## 5️⃣ (Optional) Add a **terrain** layer if you used a raster‑DEM source

```js
map.setTerrain({
  source: 'elevation',          // name of the raster‑dem source defined above
  exaggeration: 1.5
});
```

You can also add a hillshade layer:

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'hillshade',
  type: 'hillshade',
  source: 'elevation',
  paint: {
    'hillshade-shadow-color': '#000',
    'hillshade-highlight-color': '#fff',
    'hillshade-accent-color': '#555'
  }
});
```

---

## 6️⃣ Full example (HTML + JS) – copy‑paste ready

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>MapLibre + PMTiles demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.esm.js';
  import * as pmtiles from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pmtiles@3.0.0/dist/index.min.js';

  // ---- 1️⃣ Register the protocol -------------------------------------------------
  const protocol = new pmtiles.Protocol();
  maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', protocol.tile);

  // ---- 2️⃣ Create the map --------------------------------------------------------
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        world: {
          type: 'vector',
          url: 'pmtiles://https://static.example.com/world.pmtiles'
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'land',
          type: 'fill',
          source: 'world',
          'source-layer': 'land',
          paint: { 'fill-color': '#eaeaea' }
        },
        {
          id: 'water',
          type: 'fill',
          source: 'world',
          'source-layer': 'water',
          paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  // ---- 3️⃣ (Optional) Terrain ----------------------------------------------------
  // map.setTerrain({ source: 'elevation', exaggeration: 1.5 });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

*Replace `https://static.example.com/world.pmtiles` with the URL of your own archive.*

